{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tbsrb9u3pbACZT64rapKz5","type":"tool_result","content":"61:         * @description Stellar: returns an unsigned XDR to sign and submit via /v2/tx/submit. SOLANA: for an external (SIWS) wallet only, returns the unsigned transaction custody compiled, to sign with the wallet and submit via /v2/tx/submit with the same idempotencyKey. Platform-managed wallets on other chains: /v2/tx/build-sign-submit.\n132:         * @description Stellar: a signed XDR. SOLANA: the transaction /v2/tx/build returned, signed by the external wallet, with the build's idempotencyKey; custody adds the sponsor signature when the token is sponsored.\n152:         * @description Platform-managed wallets. `chain` defaults to STELLAR, which behaves exactly as v1. SOLANA takes an SPL/SOL transfer and POLYGON a POL/ERC-20 transfer, both with integer base-unit amounts and a required idempotencyKey. An external Solana wallet uses /v2/tx/build and /v2/tx/submit instead.\n267:         * @description Deprecated. Use POST /v2/tx/build-sign-submit, which is multichain and records the tx.\n10336:                    path: \"/public/v1/submit/sign_raw_payload\" | \"/public/v1/submit/sign_transaction\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_wallet_accounts\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_api_keys\" | \"/public/v1/submit/delete_api_keys\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_authenticators\" | \"/public/v1/submit/delete_authenticators\" | \"/public/v1/submit/update_user_email\" | \"/public/v1/submit/export_wallet\" | \"/public/v1/query/get_activity\" | \"/public/v1/query/get_organization\" | \"/public/v1/query/get_whoami\" | \"/public/v1/query/get_api_keys\";\n10675:                                path: \"/public/v1/submit/update_root_quorum\" | \"/public/v1/submit/delete_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_policies\";\n10775:                    path: \"/public/v1/submit/update_root_quorum\" | \"/public/v1/submit/delete_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_policies\";\n10804:                                    path: \"/public/v1/submit/update_root_quorum\" | \"/public/v1/submit/delete_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_users\" | \"/public/v1/submit/create_policies\";\n16053:     * original transport error propagates. Only ever called for GET/HEAD, so it\n16132:     * persisted key is shared per origin/API key across tabs; after another tab\n16462:     * against an sdk-api that predates `wallets[]`) have none - treat an absent\n16665:     * provider returns the user afterwards). Defaults to `window.location.origin`\n16797:    path: Extract<CosignRelayPath, '/public/v1/submit/sign_raw_payload' | '/public/v1/submit/sign_transaction' | '/public/v1/submit/create_wallet_accounts'>;\n16886:     * original user-gesture tick) don't swallow it.\n16895: * Mirrors the sdk-api `SessionsListContent` schema.\n16967:    /** API origin + version prefix (e.g. `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz/v3`). */\n17165: * via their adapter, embedded wallets sign server-side through sdk-api.\n17433: * populated on the multichain own-wallet balance (`GET /v3/wallet/balance`); the\n17434: * single-wallet lookup (`GET /v3/wallet/{publicKey}/balance`, Stellar-only) omits\n18064:    /** Forward a Turnkey request this device stamps, through sdk-api. */\n18134:     * sdk-api. Whoever holds the phrase controls every account of the wallet.\n18145: * is a Turnkey request this device stamps itself and sdk-api forwards\n18153: * Turnkey request from those checked values alone, so a compromised sdk-api\n18185:    /** One request; `sync` asks sdk-api to re-read the activity from Turnkey first. */\n18193:     * Stamp a Turnkey request with the device key and hand it to sdk-api to\n18203:     * Ask sdk-api to rebuild the request right before the vote. A transaction\n18274:     * sdk-api records the revocation when Turnkey confirms it. Revoking the key\n18285:     * ({@link checkCustodySwitchSte