{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt1aiK8k81Y558ac3q1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The app now runs on the current Pollar SDK, `@pollar/core` and `@pollar/react` at `^0.12.0`. `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, and the changes and open questions are written up in `ANSWER.md`. I checked everything against the published 0.12.0 type declarations and README. I did not run the app or call the live API.\n\nI picked 0.12.0 because it is the `latest` dist-tag. The 0.12.1 builds are only release candidates.\n\nWhat changed, by file:\n\n- **`src/pollar.ts`**: `baseUrl` was `.../v1`. In 0.12 it must be the bare origin, since the SDK adds `/v3`. Left as-is, every request would have gone to `/v1/v3`.\n- **`src/balances.ts`**: a `null` balance now shows as \"USDC unavailable\" instead of `0.00`. The `XLM` label now applies only to Stellar native coins, so other chains' native coins are not mislabelled.\n- **`src/kyc.ts`**: added the new `'expired'` status, shown as \"Verification expired\".\n- **`src/ramp.ts`**: `getRampsQuote` no longer exists. The function now reads the AR/ARS/USDC routes, quotes each one, and returns the lowest pesos-per-USDC rate, or `null` if nothing quotes. The 0.12 quote has no `rate` field, so the rate is computed as `amountIn / amountOut`.\n- **`src/trust.ts`**: the `sponsored: true` option was removed. Sponsorship is now the default, and the app's dashboard config decides who pays.\n\nOpen points, also listed in `ANSWER.md`:\n\n- **Unverified against the live API.** The ramp code assumes quote amounts are decimal strings. If they are base units, the rate is off, so one real quote response should be checked before relying on it.\n- **Ramp rail.** The new code quotes every AR/ARS/USDC rail, so the rate may now come from a different provider than before.\n- **API key.** I left `pub_testnet_tipjar_demo` unchanged and could not confirm it is still valid for the v3 API.\n- **`node_modules/`** is not in git and the repo has no `.gitignore`. I did not add one.\n\nNothing was deployed, published or sent to any service. The only network activity was read-only `npm view` and `npm install` against the public registry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1142,"cache_read_input_tokens":86714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1142},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5365cfbc-8bd5-448f-aee4-5834d27e5280","uuid":"528f2345-da11-4b28-baf4-b48cef0e5b56","timestamp":"2026-11-09T20:47:52.463Z","request_id":"req_011Cgt1ai9xsGUrSGYCNycjn"}
